cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The MSA Taxonomy: Mechanism-Signal-Archetype, a structured vocabulary for elder-fraud manipulation tactics"
message: "If you use this taxonomy, please cite it using these metadata."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Sundaar
    given-names: Ravi
    affiliation: "Sahai LLC"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-7704-4111"   # add once registered
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-08-19
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/rsundaar/msa-taxonomy"
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.REPLACE-ME"   # Zenodo mints this on first release; add it, then re-tag
abstract: >-
  A versioned, machine-readable taxonomy of the manipulation tactics used in
  fraud against older adults. Organised in three levels: mechanisms (the
  persuasion lever that explains why a target complied), signals (what can be
  observed in a contact), and archetypes (the scam families those signals
  compose into). Supporting sets cover a case-file evidence matrix and
  necessary-for-legitimacy rules for commonly impersonated institutions.
  Version 0.2.0 contains 75 entities. Every entity carries a stable identifier,
  a version, a severity, a declared theoretical grounding, and provenance
  citing the public source it rests on. Entities are deprecated rather than
  deleted and identifiers are never reused. Decision logic, detector patterns,
  and evaluation corpora are not part of this release.
keywords:
  - elder fraud
  - financial exploitation
  - scam taxonomy
  - social engineering
  - persuasion
  - older adults
  - aging in place
